data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":357,"item_id":"fc_085ba2f30e2262f6016adb231bb0208191a4853d7ca5e4e558","output_index":2,"arguments":"{\"obstacle_json\":\"{\\\"status\\\":\\\"SUSPECTED_GAP\\\",\\\"location\\\":\\\"prior-candidate.json, graph.inferences[R001].argument[S002] (lower-bound slicing step)\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The stated pointwise justification is invalid as written: from B_i⊆J_i it does not follow that the projections A_i for indices with t∈J_i cover E. The supplied completion repeats this assertion. A possible repair is to first use the true cover by indices with t∈B_i, derive the weighted pointwise lower bound using their indicators, and then dominate that sum by the measurable indicators of J_i before integration. I have not incorporated and verified that repair throughout a complete inference, nor completed the other source/dependency obligations, so I cannot responsibly submit a complete NL0 graph.\\\",\\\"basis\\\":\\\"Direct inspection of the candidate and completion text; B_i⊆J_i only gives containment of index sets in one direction and does not establish coverage at every t. This is a suspected local proof gap, not a conclusion that the theorem is false. The attempted repair is outlined above but is not a finished, audited inference.\\\",\\\"partial_progress\\\":\\\"Read all six frozen task documents and the required NL0/Yui rules including templates/submission-example.md. Probed M001 hausdorffMeasure_of_lt_dimH, M002 MeasureTheory.lintegral_tsum, M003 hausdorffMeasure_of_dimH_lt, M004 LipschitzWith.dimH_image_le, and M005 Real.dimH_of_nonempty_interior; source evidence is available in the stage case directory. M001–M005 metadata was obtained only from actual successful probes. No complete revised graph or Audit A acceptance is claimed.\\\"}\"}"}

